cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  Please cite this version of the formal proof/software release when using
  its Lean certificate. A later research article will be linked separately.
type: software
title: Finite-base Bernoulli isomorphism certificate
version: 0.1.0
authors:
  - family-names: Burton
    given-names: Peter
    email: peterburton1728@gmail.com
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  Lean certificate that there exist a countable group G and a nontrivial
  finite uniform alphabet A for which the ordinary Bernoulli shifts A^G
  and (A times A)^G are measurably conjugate on invariant conull sets.
  The algebraic input is supplied by pinned OpenAI proofs. This software
  release does not certify the manuscript's all-base or finitary extensions.
